### Area 1: profile pictures a person approves (ADR 0068).
### Sign in first (requests/auth.http), then paste the op_csrf cookie value below.
### Any signed-in person may use the routes about their own picture. The upload is
### a raw JPEG body, Content-Type image/jpeg, at most 256 KB, square, 128 to 512
### pixels a side. The server removes EXIF, GPS and every comment, and cuts
### whatever follows the end marker. A refusal carries its code in
### details[0].message (not_jpeg, damaged, not_square, wrong_size, ...).
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@csrf = paste the op_csrf cookie value here after signing in
@pictureId = paste a picture id from the answer to GET mine

### What you have: the approved picture, the one waiting for review, the last
### decision against you, and how many uploads you have left in 24 hours.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/profile-pictures/mine

### Send a picture for review. The body is the file itself, a checked-in flat
### colour square made in code. A new upload replaces your pending picture.
### The AI check does not run under today's data rule: pending.ai.status says so.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/profile-pictures/mine
Content-Type: image/jpeg
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

< ../test/fixtures/profile-picture-flat-256.jpg

### Take back your own picture, waiting or approved. Taking back a picture that is
### already gone answers the same way and changes nothing.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/profile-pictures/{{pictureId}}/withdraw
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### The bytes of one picture. Any signed-in person may ask for an approved one. A
### pending one is shown only to its owner (in a demo session, the sign-in that
### sent it) and to whoever holds users.manage; anyone else, and a rejected,
### removed or taken-down picture, gets 404. The answer is private and revalidated
### every time: the ETag is the picture's SHA-256, so a repeat with
### If-None-Match answers 304 only while the picture is still visible.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/profile-pictures/{{pictureId}}/image
If-None-Match: "paste the ETag of the last answer"
